AUDIO: 'chart anything cuz this might just change how models and languages work together. The project is called Flint and the idea clicks once you see the chart generation'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is secretly two jobs. Job one is meaning this column is month, that one\'s revenue and that one\'s a percentage change. LLMs nail that. Job two is geometry. Axis, step sizes, scale domains, label'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'spacing, color ramps. LLMs are bad sometimes at geometry. And that\'s exactly where your generated charts kind of die off. The Flint team hits this wall themselves, building their own analytics agent that measured roughly'

[01:06] [scene:transition]
VISUAL: A dark screen with a subtle purple glow.
AUDIO: '80% success on good-looking charts. Sounds decent until real users are on the other end, and one in five charts is broken. So, Flint splits the jobs into two. The model writes about 10 lines of JSON that only describe meaning using'

